# The fort: a hall, ten doors, and somebody behind each of them.
#
#     build\RatnaBay.exe --yard --script Docs\scripts\clip-fort.rbs
#     powershell -File tools\make-clips.ps1
#
# This is the clip the console records well, and it is worth being clear about why.
# A scripted fight is a poor performance -- the swings are on a timer rather than
# on a read of the room, and the console cannot aim -- but walking through a place
# is exactly what a script does honestly. The fort is thirty metres of lit hall
# with a figure standing in every chamber, and that reads on its own.

descend 1 20789
wait 0.5
surface
wait 1

goto fort
wait 0.5
look 4.712 0
use
wait 1.2

record captures/clip-fort 10 30

# Down the hall to the chamber at z=0, which is 18 metres at 6 m/s.
#
# Timed from the geometry rather than guessed. The first cut walked 3.2 seconds --
# 19.2 metres -- which stopped 1.2 metres past the doorway's centre line, and since
# a doorway is 3 metres wide the turn met a jamb. Every chamber centre is a
# multiple of the 7-metre pitch from a spawn at z=18, so the walk that lands on one
# is arithmetic, not trial and error.
walk 3.0
where

# Turn into it. Yaw is radians and 3*pi/2 looks down -X, which is the west side.
look 4.712 0
wait 0.7

# In to the occupant: 9.1 metres from the middle of the hall to where they stand.
walk 1.45
wait 0.4

# And what they have to say.
use
wait 3

quit
